Kreative Studio pose editor (STU-PE1). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.


Write public/js/pose/ops.js (NAME = ops), the JSON op API of the pose editor. Use need('skeleton','./skeleton.js'), need('fk','./fk.js'), need('ik','./ik.js'), need('lookat','./lookat.js') and need('presets','./presets.js') inside the functions (S, FK, IK, LA, PR below).

A pose is {version: 1, root: {pos: [x,y,z]}, joints: {name: {bend, side, twist}}} (degrees). Export:
- clamp(name, e): returns {bend, side, twist} with each value (missing = 0) clamped to S.byName[name].limits[k] = [lo, hi], written as (x || 0) so -0 becomes 0.
- apply(pose, ops): ops is one op object or an array of them. Work on a deep copy (JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(pose))); never change the input. Returns {pose, notes}, notes = array of strings.
Every joint value that gets stored goes through store(p, name, e, notes): c = clamp(name, e); for each k in bend, side, twist where the wanted value (e[k] || 0) differs from c[k] by more than 1e-9, push `${name} ${k} ${round1(e[k])} limited to ${c[k]}` (round1 = Math.round(x * 10) / 10); then p.joints[name] = c.
Ops (op.op):
- set_joint {joint, bend?, side?, twist?, add?}: unknown joint -> throw new Error(`Unknown joint "${joint}".`); each given field must be a finite number else throw new Error(`${k} must be a number.`). Start from the current values (0 when missing); given fields replace them, or are added when add is true. store().
- curl_finger {hand, finger, amount}: hand must be 'l', 'r' or 'both' (else 'hand must be l, r or both.'); finger one of S.FINGERS keys or 'all' (else 'finger must be thumb, index, middle, ring, pinky or all.'); amount a number in 0..1 (else 'amount must be between 0 and 1.'). For every chosen side s and finger f and joint j in S.FINGERS[f]: name = `${s}_${j}`, keep its side and twist, bend = amount * S.byName[name].limits.bend[1]; store().
- mirror {from}: 'l' or 'r' copies that side onto the other: delete every joints entry of the other side, then for every entry of the from side store(p, S.mirrorName(name), copy). 'swap': build new joints where l_ and r_ entries trade names (values unchanged), and entries of other joints get side and twist negated (as 0 - x || 0); root.pos[0] = 0 - root.pos[0] || 0. Else throw 'from must be l, r or swap.'.
- look_at: r = LA.lookAt(p, op); store() each of r.joints.
- ik {chain, target, pole?}: unknown chain -> 'chain must be l_arm, r_arm, l_leg or r_leg.' (check IK.CHAINS before calling). r = IK.solve(p, op); store() each of r.joints; when !r.reached push `${op.chain} cannot reach the target`.
- move_root {pos}: pos must be 3 finite numbers (else 'pos must be [x, y, z].'); p.root.pos = copy of pos.
- reset {joints?}: without joints p becomes FK.defaultPose(); with joints delete those entries.
- preset {name}: PR.PRESETS[name] missing -> throw new Error(`Unknown preset "${name}". Use one of: ${Object.keys(PR.PRESETS).join(', ')}.`). Else p becomes the result of apply(FK.defaultPose(), PR.PRESETS[name]).pose and its notes are added.
- anything else: throw new Error(`Unknown op "${op.op}". Use one of: set_joint, curl_finger, mirror, look_at, ik, move_root, reset, preset.`).
Remove joint entries whose three values are all 0 at the very end (so a pose at rest has joints {}).
